notes               = "Untitled in source. IMPORTANT — the ===lantern=== on this poem is BEN'S OWN pencil rendering from the margin of the printed page, not an agent's; his spelling of 'persistance' is reproduced as written. This follows the page-70 / stay-go precedent. Note he reads دوام آوردیم ('we held out, we endured') as a thing brought TO the pigeons, which the Persian does not quite say; the literal machine pass keeps the idiom. Four lines, and a companion to dove-apprentice (126) — the doves are what the surviving was for. 26 Bahman = 14 February 1997. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

ما نرفتیم...
دوام آوردیم...
تا کبوترها را...
از دلِ چاه... به بام آوردیم...
۱۳۷۵/۱۱/۲۶

===machine===

We did not go...
we held out...
until the doves...
from the heart of the well... we brought up to the roof...
1375/11/26

===lantern===

we didn't go
we brought persistance
to pigeons

from the hearts of wells
to the roof tops
we bring it in

===translation===

